1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
How so? I'll give you an example

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,280
When I compare myself with another person

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,000
Are we similar? No

4
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:13,360
When comparing on either of us have better achievements

5
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,240
Can you guarantee to me that he isn't standing on a box?

6
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:21,360
And guarantee to me that he isn't standing in a hole

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,640
I don't know what their conditions are

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,680
So, if we are both different, then the comparison is invalid

9
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,480
The comparisons between two different things are invalid

10
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,480
Since we are both different, then it's invalid

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,160
Okay, secondly...

12
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,640
The comparison with another person is invalid

13
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,200
Because comparisons are required but non-binding

14
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:40,480
Required but non-binding

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:44,600
Meaning that, I compare myself to take guidance

16
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,040
Not to judge myself

17
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:53,240
That's why comparisons have four types in terms of impact and results

18
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:57,560
There are the ascending and descending comparisons

19
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,960
The positive and negative impact

20
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,960
Those are the four types

21
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:06,640
The ascending comparison with a positive impact

22
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,640
Is what inspires me

23
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:11,320
When I compare myself to some higher than me

24
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,920
You're good and skilled with podcasts

25
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,240
The positive impact is when it inspires me

26
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:18,040
To follow suit as him

27
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,040
This is the ascending comparison

28
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:21,680
That has a positive impact

29
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:25,000
This is the difference between both

30
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:29,320
People should seek to become better

31
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,200
Not to become the best

32
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:35,480
Why? why not become the best?

33
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:39,000
Because seeking this will ruin your principles

34
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,520
And will make you enemies, and will cause you to burn out

35
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:45,160
And you'll belittle Allah's favors to you

36
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,160
And it defies the rules of the universe

37
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,560
When you seek to become The Best

38
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:54,360
By this, you'll be competing with the destiny of the others

39
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,680
Not the others, because it is their destiny

40
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,680
This is their fate, you can't compete with that

41
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,740
Rather, seek to be better, work on yourself

42
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:02,380
Don't compare yourself with others

43
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:05,460
There's a story that I might have mentioned before

44
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,460
I'll mention it in this context

45
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:11,980
About the man who sells chicks

46
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:13,700
Dancing chicks

47
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:18,900
He played music, and the chicks were dancing

48
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,540
And people came and bought from him

49
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,820
One of them returned home and played music for the chick to dance but it didn't

50
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,220
He tried but with it didn't dance

51
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,220
He changed the music, and it still didn't dance

52
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,940
He returned to the seller and found everyone gathered back there

53
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,940
And the seller had vanished

54
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:38,220
The seller did a trick

55
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:44,140
That the plate on which the chicks were on was heated

56
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:48,700
So, the chicks would raise their legs

57
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:55,260
And with music, it appeared to people that the chicks were dancing

58
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:00,100
People here bought the chicks, but not the plate

59
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,700
And what made the chicks dance was the plate

60
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:07,700
So, when you want to live the life of another person

61
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:11,140
Or the idea or the attitude of another person

62
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,420
You would be like those who took the chick

63
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:18,100
But you can't take the plate

64
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:21,180
You can't... Because it represents Allah's destiny

65
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:24,380
It could represent his mother's faithful prayers to him

66
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,580
It could represent Allah's trial to him

67
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:30,220
Because Allah might also trial people with favors and success

68
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,360
It could represent his upbringing

69
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:36,780
It could represent unseen charity or prayers

70
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,540
You can't know, and you can't get this

71
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:41,420
That's why, you shouldn't seek out what's out of your reach

72
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:45,060
Keep with yourself, strive to become better

73
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,260
Not to become the best
